  it's a is a phenomenal idea because what  this does is it leads to adam beshear  taking off to the moon presumably to see  the watcher we're not entirely sure but  he's suddenly met by the arrival of  conor simps and the the discussion  between the two of them really breaks  out insofar as there's a a bit of a  personal vendetta here in the sense that  because of what conor sims became  because of how violent he became and how  terrible he became insofar as wanting to  eliminate the entirety of humanity right  or force humanity to change that what  adam beshear did is he actually  organized the the wife and child of  conor sims to be moved to a safe  location so conor couldn't get to them  but conor saw it as adam bashir standing  in the way and actually preventing him  or at least taking away the things that  meant the most to him and so that's when  adam tells conor he says things are  better conor not like they were in like  the 60s they're not perfect but there  are good people on all sides who are  trying to come together you have to  believe in that and the response of  conor is that belief is misplaced and  you are naive for having it adam he says  i've walked this world in the short time  i've been back and that is far from true  everywhere i look man still hates his  brother be it the south the far east or  the middle east it's all the same adam  and it's your weakness that allowed all  of this and when adam asked the question  is it really my weakness that i chose  peace over violence the response of  conor is no it's because you chose to  turn your back when it was within your  power to stop this madness millions of  your own people left to suffer under the  yoke of oppression little girls who were  burned in churches by professed  believers men hung from trees like  strange fruit because they dared to look  their oppressors in the eye if you had  done something then perhaps i would not  have to do anything now and that's  really the crux and the nature of conor  sims one of the best things about this  story is that anti-man is not some kind  of villain of the weak guy it's not all  man i have these kind of anti-matter  powers i'm sure i'm a little bit  unstable in terms of my powers but i'm  gonna conquer the world because i love  having power no it's not like that and  in fact it's the other philosophical  side of the equation a more extreme  equation but still a logical equation  right the stance of conor sims and is  exactly what we talked about in the  first video the stance of conor sims is  that if humanity wanted to change  humanity would have changed there's  nothing stopping the human race from  changing but it's not like thanos used  the mind stone and is forcing humanity  to fight against itself you know based  on petty squabbles like skin color or  religious convictions or socioeconomic  status right it's humanity that chooses  to do that to itself the stance of conor  sims at least in this story is that's  how people are people don't want  anything to get better adam bashir and  your belief in the fact that they do is  foolhardy what you're doing here is  you're looking for reasons to believe  that humanity wants to be better in the  face of the fact that they don't now the  other part of this equation is that  conor sims has a huge negativity bias  because if adam bashir is basically  looking for reasons to believe why  humanity is worth saving conor sims is  looking for reasons to believe that it's  not and so both of these guys if if  we're being honest here neither one of  them is actually right but the truth is  they're both operating on two opposites  right then you have adam beshear who's  operating as an extreme optimist and  you've got conor since who's operating  as an extreme pessimist the question  that really has to be asked here is  based on these two ideologies if you had  to choose one which one would be right i  would argue that it's one of those  things where if humanity truly wasn't  worth saving then there would be no  volunteers there'd be no charity there'd  be there wouldn't be anybody out there  doing anything that's good the reality  is that there are people who are doing  that now ultimately conor sims gets the  upper hand on adam beshear knocks him  unconscious and says you had your time  adam you could have fixed the world you  could have made it better but you chose  not to and so in the face of the fact  that humanity will not fix itself i will  make humanity fix itself with that being  said guys we're gonna bring this video  to an end thank you all for watching and  i will catch you all later  peace
 

